planEntities.description:
BES-NET supported:
Sea-grass pollination research;
Establishment of butterfly gardens and pollinator displays in the Botanical Gardens of Trinidad as well as Tobago;
Testing of honey at various aviaries throughout Trinidad & Tobago to assist in the development of a quality standard for stingless bee honey;
Bat pollination research;
Development of pollinator protocols;
Development of local plants and pollinators database;
Development of a Theory of Change for a Pollinator Conservation Strategy;
Drafting of guidelines for the management of stingless bees;
Design and implementation of a public awareness campaign on pollinators and pollination

GEF SGP supported: 
Conduct pollinator surveys in North East Trinidad and Tobago; 
Research study to identify types of bee species in Trinidad & Tobago;
Pollinator workshops

(Project start date pre-dates MSDCF 2022-2026: 01-06-2020)

Workshop retraining of staff within the energy sector; drafting of a national policy that integrates RE;
Public awareness campaign to sensitize the public to RE, EE and energy pricing based on studies and surveys of RE awareness and acceptance;
Eight (8) PV demonstration installation projects in rural/remote communities supportive of CSOs/NGO
(Project start date pre-dates the MSDCF 2022-2026: 31-03-2019)

Establish a GBV hotline where survivors of violence are moved along a continuum of care to access appropriate medical and
psychosocial support services including: 
(A) Counselling (Psychologist) - for survivors of violence, those at risk of experiencing
violence and those who have experienced trauma because of violence; 
(B) Case Management; 
(C) Emergency Contraception and
other critical interventions within the Clinical Management of Rape package; 
(D) Contraceptives information and commodities;
(E)Doctor's Consultation; 
(F) Registered Nurse (RN) Consultation/Counselling; 
(G) Outbound/Extremal Referrals. When needed, survivors will be offered Dignity kits.

